{
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "text": "What does elif add after an if?",
      "options": [
        "Another condition, checked only when the ones above it are false",
        "A block that always runs after the if",
        "A second program that runs at the same time",
        "A condition that is checked before the if"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "text": "In an if / elif / else chain that ends with an else, how many blocks run?",
      "options": [
        "Every block whose condition is true",
        "All of them, from top to bottom",
        "Exactly one: the first block whose condition is true, or the else when none is",
        "The last block whose condition is true"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "text": "Several conditions of a chain are true. Which block runs?",
      "options": [
        "The last true one",
        "The first true one, from the top",
        "Every true one, one after another",
        "None: Python stops with an error"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "text": "Once a block of the chain has run, what does the program do?",
      "options": [
        "It checks the next elif too",
        "It runs the else as well",
        "It starts the chain again from the top",
        "It leaves the chain and goes on with the line after it"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "text": "When does the else at the end of a chain run?",
      "options": [
        "When no if or elif above it is true",
        "Every time, after the other blocks",
        "Only when the if is false, whatever the elifs say",
        "When the last elif is false, even if the if was true"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "text": "When does the lesson say to chain if / elif / else?",
      "options": [
        "Whenever a program has more than two conditions",
        "When we want every condition to be checked",
        "When we test the same variable for several cases",
        "Only when the conditions use =="
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "text": "Which of these lines is right?",
      "options": [
        "else if seconds == 60:",
        "elif seconds == 60:",
        "elif seconds == 60",
        "elif: seconds == 60"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "text": "Where can an elif go?",
      "options": [
        "Anywhere in the program, on its own",
        "After the else",
        "Before the if",
        "Right after the block of an if or of another elif"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q9",
      "text": "Does a chain need an else at the end?",
      "options": [
        "No, but without it nothing runs when no condition is true",
        "Yes, Python stops with an error without it",
        "Yes, otherwise the elif lines are skipped",
        "No, and without it every elif block runs"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q10",
      "text": "How many elif can a chain have?",
      "options": [
        "Only one",
        "At most three",
        "As many as we need",
        "As many as the variables we check"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q11",
      "text": "Why does this print two lines?",
      "code": "seconds = 60\nif seconds == 100:\n    print(\"Starting the computers\")\nif seconds == 60:\n    print(\"Checking the tower\")\nif seconds < 10:\n    print(\"Taking off\")\nelse:\n    print(\"No effect\")",
      "options": [
        "An else always runs at the end of a program",
        "The else belongs only to the last if, and seconds < 10 is false",
        "seconds == 60 is checked twice",
        "Every if runs its block, true or not"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q12",
      "text": "What is wrong with this chain?",
      "code": "score = 95\nif score >= 50:\n    print(\"Pass\")\nelif score >= 90:\n    print(\"Excellent\")",
      "options": [
        "Nothing, it prints Excellent for 95",
        "An elif needs an else after it",
        "It prints both Pass and Excellent for 95",
        "Excellent never prints: a score of 90 or more already passes the first check"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q13",
      "text": "A score of 90 or more is Excellent, 50 or more is Pass. In which order do we check?",
      "options": [
        "score >= 90 in the if, then score >= 50 in the elif",
        "score >= 50 in the if, then score >= 90 in the elif",
        "score >= 50 in the if, then score >= 90 in the else",
        "Any order, the chain prints the same"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q14",
      "text": "What is the difference between three ifs one after another and an if / elif / elif chain?",
      "options": [
        "None, they always print the same",
        "Separate ifs are all checked; a chain stops at its first true condition",
        "In a chain the elifs are checked before the if",
        "Separate ifs stop at their first true condition"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q15",
      "text": "In the lesson's rocket, with seconds = 60, which conditions does Python check?",
      "options": [
        "Only seconds == 60",
        "All of them, then it picks seconds == 60",
        "seconds == 100, then seconds == 60, then it leaves the chain",
        "seconds == 60, then all the ones below it"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q16",
      "text": "In the lesson's rocket, what is printed with seconds = 45?",
      "options": [
        "Starting secondary engines",
        "Checking connection with the control tower",
        "Nothing: 45 matches no condition",
        "45 seconds has no effect"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q17",
      "text": "In the lesson's rocket, with seconds = 9, what decides the line that is printed?",
      "options": [
        "The if inside elif seconds < 10, which checks error_detected",
        "Only the else at the end of the chain",
        "seconds == 10, since 9 is close to 10",
        "Nothing: 9 matches no condition"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q18",
      "text": "What do we call an if written inside the block of another if, elif or else?",
      "options": ["An elif", "A chained if", "A nested if", "A double condition"],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q19",
      "text": "How far is the block of a nested if indented?",
      "options": [
        "As far left as the outer if",
        "One step more than the nested if line itself",
        "As far as the nested if line itself",
        "Not at all, it is already inside a block"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q20",
      "text": "In the Oxygen Level Monitor mission, what does the station print with oxygen = 79?",
      "options": [
        "Oxygen low - conserve power",
        "Oxygen nominal",
        "Oxygen critical - seal the bay",
        "Oxygen nominal and Oxygen low - conserve power"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q21",
      "text": "In the Oxygen Level Monitor mission, what does the station print with oxygen = 12 and crew_aboard = False?",
      "options": [
        "Emergency - evacuate now",
        "Oxygen critical - seal the bay",
        "Nothing, since the crew is not aboard",
        "We have no crew aboard, so venting the bay is safe"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q22",
      "text": "The mission's chain starts with `if oxygen >= 80:`. Which line checks for 50 to 79?",
      "options": [
        "if oxygen >= 50:",
        "elif oxygen <= 79:",
        "elif oxygen >= 50:",
        "elif oxygen > 50:"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q23",
      "text": "Why doesn't `elif oxygen >= 50:` also need to check that oxygen is below 80?",
      "options": [
        "Python checks the 80 by itself at the end",
        "The elif is checked only when oxygen >= 80 was false, so oxygen is already below 80",
        "Because 50 is less than 80, Python skips the check",
        "It does need to: 90 would print Oxygen low too"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q24",
      "text": "Is the else reached when x is 5?",
      "code": "x = 5\nif x > 10:\n    print(\"Big\")\nelif x > 0:\n    print(\"Small\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Zero or less\")",
      "options": [
        "Yes, the else always runs at the end",
        "Yes, because x > 10 is false",
        "No: x > 0 is true, so the chain stops there",
        "No, Python stops with an error first"
      ],
      "answer": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "q25",
      "text": "What happens when this runs?",
      "code": "x = 3\nelif x > 0:\n    print(\"Positive\")",
      "options": [
        "It stops with an error: an elif needs an if before it",
        "It prints Positive",
        "It prints nothing",
        "It prints 3"
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "q26",
      "text": "What happens when this runs?",
      "code": "x = 3\nif x > 5:\n    print(\"Big\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Small\")\nelif x > 0:\n    print(\"Positive\")",
      "options": [
        "It prints Small",
        "It prints Small, then Positive",
        "It prints Positive",
        "It stops with an error: an elif can't come after the else"
      ],
      "answer": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "q27",
      "text": "Which program prints exactly one line, whatever number temperature holds?",
      "options": [
        "if temperature < 0:\n    print(\"Ice\")\nif temperature < 20:\n    print(\"Cool\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Warm\")",
        "if temperature < 0:\n    print(\"Ice\")\nelif temperature < 20:\n    print(\"Cool\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Warm\")",
        "if temperature < 0:\n    print(\"Ice\")\nelif temperature < 20:\n    print(\"Cool\")",
        "if temperature < 0:\n    print(\"Ice\")\nelif temperature < 20:\n    print(\"Cool\")\nprint(\"Warm\")"
      ],
      "answer": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "q28",
      "text": "In `elif seconds < 10:  # the last 10 seconds`, what does the comment do?",
      "options": [
